[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-110367"] :question/problem "Let $D=[0,2]\\times [0,2].$ Which of the following functions are valid joint probability density functions?\n\n- $f(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x+y,\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$\n- $g(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}-xy,\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$\n- $h(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}xy,\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nLet's check the above conditions for each of the given functions.\n\n- The function $f$ is *not* a valid probability density function because it does not satisfy the second condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\text{ }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+xy]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(2y+2)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[{y}^{2}+2y]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =8 \\\\  & \\ne 1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $g$ is *not* a valid probability density function because it does not satisfy the first condition. For example,\n\n$$\ng(1,2)=-1\\cdot 2=-2≱0.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The function $h$ is a valid probability density function. Indeed, we have $h(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$  and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}h(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}h(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}xy\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{4}xy\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\cdot y]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$h$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-110859/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "d171dd14-8615-5b1b-bec7-495a172fa49e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110859/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "274d1bf4-550a-5376-af5b-69398c7a0395" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110859/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b638da0d-3d68-5730-af19-6b5c1e473d41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110859/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c12cf603-6fa4-5a75-b5ff-34e1d8e148fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110859/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "321b39cb-f323-586e-939f-01055e7dc783" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110859/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d436e34-c899-5f14-b432-318089e23847" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110859/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-110859/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-110859/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-110859/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-110859/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-110859/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110859" :question/id #uuid "58750b94-7cd1-58aa-8aff-a1750f03442c" :question/math-academy-id "q-110859" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{(1+x+y)^{3}},\\, & x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/996bd092be07e2596e30739cc4249e8ed8ef859540067a94e0f9cdd05f9e1f84.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{c}{(1+x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }[{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{c}{(1+x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{[-\\frac{c}{2(1+x+y)^{2}}]}_{y=0}^{y=\\infty }\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{c}{2(1+x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{c}{2(1+x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-\\frac{c}{2(1+x)}]}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{2}=1\\,⇒\\,c=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-110859/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a66952d-4e4b-5249-8f44-27d6fd198ea8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110859"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110865/selection/54260034644bf2398d955582fcfe14cc95cc4887ad666376368d8327ed5e3102" :answer/id #uuid "bcdf2e30-e13d-5c81-84ec-063b0ed08d4c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$g$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110865/selection/bb292cda762e5b8cdec132334ba43c76a2cfaab9cfffc89bd50f767fb9b03a74" :answer/id #uuid "5b8b81d9-2ee8-577f-abf8-fd33080cec08" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110865/selection/2a1d8a89f00ace1b1ddd51d9e5ff705929e76b6edeee97f394d666550954368a" :answer/id #uuid "51dc79cc-c2d6-50ee-bdcc-aa1eee7a9b86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$h$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110865/selection/9af10456e8aaa200b7ffe625b2da3a488db9dd53569041e400767aa22135d465" :answer/id #uuid "164cfb7d-c0d3-59d5-8786-d7eba5b7d60d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f,$ $g,$ and $h$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110865/selection/8179e352607fde1d20643aaf2dd5550f91f25ca3d0bbbef167f92cf9dc7a168e" :answer/id #uuid "5aae3cfb-3787-5d5a-a14d-8c040b49edf5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$g$ and $h$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110865/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f112021-2a00-5cbb-b61a-d38df35ef7f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110865/selection/2a1d8a89f00ace1b1ddd51d9e5ff705929e76b6edeee97f394d666550954368a" :answer-field/choices ["q-110865/selection/54260034644bf2398d955582fcfe14cc95cc4887ad666376368d8327ed5e3102" "q-110865/selection/bb292cda762e5b8cdec132334ba43c76a2cfaab9cfffc89bd50f767fb9b03a74" "q-110865/selection/2a1d8a89f00ace1b1ddd51d9e5ff705929e76b6edeee97f394d666550954368a" "q-110865/selection/9af10456e8aaa200b7ffe625b2da3a488db9dd53569041e400767aa22135d465" "q-110865/selection/8179e352607fde1d20643aaf2dd5550f91f25ca3d0bbbef167f92cf9dc7a168e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110865" :question/id #uuid "ffd90769-db03-5a84-9839-38f6442c5a87" :question/math-academy-id "q-110865" :question/problem "Let $D=[0,2]\\times [0,1].$ Which of the following functions are valid joint probability density functions?\n\n- $f(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$\n- $g(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}x-y,\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$\n- $h(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}xy,\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nLet's check the above conditions for each of the given functions.\n\n- The function $f$ is *not* a valid probability density function because it does not satisfy the second condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[3x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[2{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & \\ne 1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $g$ is *not* a valid probability density function because it does not satisfy the first condition. For example,\n\n$$\ng(0,1)=0-1=-1≱0.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- The function $h$ is a valid probability density function. Indeed, we have $h(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$  and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}h(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}h(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}xy\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\cdot y]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$h$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110865/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a66952d-4e4b-5249-8f44-27d6fd198ea8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110865"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110862/selection/bb292cda762e5b8cdec132334ba43c76a2cfaab9cfffc89bd50f767fb9b03a74" :answer/id #uuid "3fc6c4b4-549b-5687-986d-ce9b99e3a5b6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110862/selection/0c1ca63c3c6c805ef06c7bcf31ae0d5219aad8d8f314916c203a48f8e14c7d02" :answer/id #uuid "d855dda0-1832-54f3-b5fc-b49ed6097c80" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f$ and $g$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110862/selection/8179e352607fde1d20643aaf2dd5550f91f25ca3d0bbbef167f92cf9dc7a168e" :answer/id #uuid "64549d8e-0810-5f37-902d-0e1867f455f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$g$ and $h$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110862/selection/c820fc75b83ab642062caecaa665e20c3efdace607db6b590468cae51c449859" :answer/id #uuid "74c21183-a94b-5f13-bdba-d3f7b89e2204" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$f$ and $h$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110862/selection/54260034644bf2398d955582fcfe14cc95cc4887ad666376368d8327ed5e3102" :answer/id #uuid "ac2baaa1-d256-57c1-b9b8-3ccaa249e88b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$g$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110862/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3017f8be-9b1b-512e-af57-df5318abf3aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110862/selection/0c1ca63c3c6c805ef06c7bcf31ae0d5219aad8d8f314916c203a48f8e14c7d02" :answer-field/choices ["q-110862/selection/bb292cda762e5b8cdec132334ba43c76a2cfaab9cfffc89bd50f767fb9b03a74" "q-110862/selection/0c1ca63c3c6c805ef06c7bcf31ae0d5219aad8d8f314916c203a48f8e14c7d02" "q-110862/selection/8179e352607fde1d20643aaf2dd5550f91f25ca3d0bbbef167f92cf9dc7a168e" "q-110862/selection/c820fc75b83ab642062caecaa665e20c3efdace607db6b590468cae51c449859" "q-110862/selection/54260034644bf2398d955582fcfe14cc95cc4887ad666376368d8327ed5e3102"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110862" :question/id #uuid "061bd00a-a3a9-5962-aa57-6ff275a6b065" :question/math-academy-id "q-110862" :question/problem "Let $D=[0,2]\\times [1,2].$ Which of the following functions are valid joint probability density functions?\n\n- $f(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{3},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$\n- $g(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$\n- $h(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-y}{6},\\, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nLet's check the above conditions for each of the given functions.\n\n- The function $f$ is a valid probability density function. Indeed, we have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$  and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{y}{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{y}{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{xy}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{2y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $g$ is a valid probability density function. Indeed, we have $g(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$  and\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{R}^{2}}g(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{D}g(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}1\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[y]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The function $h$ is *not* a valid probability density function because it does not satisfy the first condition. For example,\n\n$$\nh(0,2)=\\frac{0-2}{6}=-\\frac{1}{3}≱0.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$f$ and $g$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110862/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a66952d-4e4b-5249-8f44-27d6fd198ea8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110862"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110858/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "f564f0d3-7c7d-5d82-87a3-d13c59c706c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110858/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" :answer/id #uuid "00f67b2b-134e-58b3-93ae-fa7ba28c4140" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110858/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0d83fa88-d874-5f98-9227-e0ffb8353e79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110858/selection/be7671dfcec88fd83021721c027e180f94aa5dc830cb53553598c14eaf369bc4" :answer/id #uuid "28da754e-ef87-574a-8792-4fd2fb2dd9cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{e}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110858/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3cf3110c-8a14-53b0-9c2c-458aeb4dabb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110858/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b657716-d94a-5e07-8159-82a0683c8d63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110858/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-110858/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-110858/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" "q-110858/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-110858/selection/be7671dfcec88fd83021721c027e180f94aa5dc830cb53553598c14eaf369bc4" "q-110858/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110858" :question/id #uuid "5ae02804-fba0-5c96-b940-671c232a4a2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-110858" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}c{e}^{-x-y},\\, & x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/996bd092be07e2596e30739cc4249e8ed8ef859540067a94e0f9cdd05f9e1f84.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }c{e}^{-x-y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }[{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }c{e}^{-x-y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }[-c{e}^{-x-y}]_{y=0}^{y=\\infty }\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }c{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }c{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =[-c{e}^{-x}]_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-110858/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1a66952d-4e4b-5249-8f44-27d6fd198ea8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110858"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110986/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "8890274b-e436-55ab-9e10-c911c0ce5a24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110986/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "88ad20ec-8a48-5821-9c61-28fecb88e386" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110986/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "3ce47bd2-d131-57c5-9920-86fc56d7b67a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110986/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "cc27a050-cb0f-5a7c-a98f-f849a38f9b01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110986/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "628c13fb-158f-577f-8098-bb8cdbd706ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110986/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d84369d4-8ad0-581d-af0c-bf33c588aa07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110986/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-110986/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-110986/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-110986/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-110986/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-110986/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110986" :question/id #uuid "86d22edc-bcdf-5bbd-9aca-23ca6a278347" :question/math-academy-id "q-110986" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y},\\, & 1\\le x\\le e,\\,e\\le y\\le {e}^{x}, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,e\\le y\\le {e}^{x}}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/268e469b0306d22e6b6dc05905a9d56a1cabd4b0e405f741ff458ca241440d4a.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{c}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx=1.\n$$\n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{c}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{c}{yx\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{c}{x}[{\\int }_{e}^{{e}^{x}}\\frac{1}{y\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}\\,dy]\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{c}{x}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)]_{y=e}^{y={e}^{x}}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{c}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{x})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}dx & ={[\\frac{c{ln}^{2}⁡x}{2}]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{c{ln}^{2}⁡e}{2}-\\frac{c{ln}^{2}⁡1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{2}=1\\,⇒\\,c=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110986/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "129940fb-a409-55bc-9852-f68f4f9ffd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110986"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-110366"] :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}cxy,\\, & 0\\le x\\le y<1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le y<1}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/01f3a8d99dd38ce2a728fe2cb4e4ab8de933ccd9ba27c87174779c428c303f48.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1}cxy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{x}^{1}cxy\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[cx\\cdot \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=x}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{cx}{2}-\\frac{c{x}^{3}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{cx}{2}-\\frac{c{x}^{3}}{2})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{c{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{c{x}^{4}}{8}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{4}-\\frac{c}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{8}=1\\,⇒\\,c=8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-110868/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "ca8d5bab-89a6-5916-a4fc-95cf72781446" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110868/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0dcce90f-9727-5493-b402-5e32257e78d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110868/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "641f6abf-13c9-55f1-80ab-517f544afec9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110868/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "7ddb0b2a-ff3f-5a75-9784-1c07d72a70aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110868/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "feb721c9-f6aa-5036-9268-8d211fed143a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110868/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9fd94a9-f00c-5b19-8e86-4e6c811991b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110868/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-110868/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-110868/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-110868/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-110868/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-110868/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110868" :question/id #uuid "f8890e3b-d9f0-5edf-8858-b6864ec3a81c" :question/math-academy-id "q-110868" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y),\\, & 0\\le y\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/a49e679b3919594edc7fe963190a754324b9b5ea980d1936121c040d0ee52284.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nW\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{[-c\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)]}_{y=0}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-c\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+c\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(c\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-c\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={[c\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{c\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )}{2} \\\\  & =c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nc=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-110868/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "129940fb-a409-55bc-9852-f68f4f9ffd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110868"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110985/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "ef682d15-9356-56f8-9b5e-fb3bc7b79e9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110985/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "d4306db3-86b1-5a7e-a5b5-042ff9ada147" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110985/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "ec1417ee-51dc-5a94-8125-0d178934c10b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110985/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "a708adde-bd6b-52a1-9f62-e622df87e411" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110985/selection/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1" :answer/id #uuid "76fbf73e-36cb-55ba-b6b0-cce8a0e64238" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110985/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5fe3691-1723-5a5c-8d1e-b7506d0e0249" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110985/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-110985/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-110985/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" "q-110985/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-110985/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-110985/selection/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110985" :question/id #uuid "0936abbb-9e50-567c-890d-40631da84483" :question/math-academy-id "q-110985" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}c(1-xy),\\, & {y}^{2}\\le x\\le y, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le y}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/1ef0c7b289e24a98366c64b9a213c4f67d2fc63157b3319f0118eb16c514097e.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}c(1-xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating  $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}c(1-xy)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[cx-\\frac{cy{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x={y}^{2}}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}c(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-({y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2}))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}c(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-{y}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c(y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2}-{y}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{5}}{2})\\,dy & =c{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{6}}{12}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{2}-\\frac{c}{8}-\\frac{c}{3}+\\frac{c}{12}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{c}{8}=1\\,⇒\\,c=8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110985/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "129940fb-a409-55bc-9852-f68f4f9ffd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110985"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-110987/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "1ab3e703-0277-5209-8933-cb51ec37c29c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110987/selection/75be7144d0f06979df25a4d833026b673a3f8e67075b82357bb7a90b42abaa01" :answer/id #uuid "4c9eec72-68d9-541e-86d5-d914b897362b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110987/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "50cb7ee5-d867-59a5-bd04-b6654c703374" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110987/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "0e504688-fa64-5b33-a8f9-11418206011e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110987/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "f819e9ff-0b47-50ad-910d-611d3a426d79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-110987/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5dba9fcb-0c02-5b23-966d-2cd3ae950928" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-110987/selection/75be7144d0f06979df25a4d833026b673a3f8e67075b82357bb7a90b42abaa01" :answer-field/choices ["q-110987/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-110987/selection/75be7144d0f06979df25a4d833026b673a3f8e67075b82357bb7a90b42abaa01" "q-110987/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" "q-110987/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-110987/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-110987" :question/id #uuid "ebb42d17-0dc1-5df4-b258-bdc2fae854db" :question/math-academy-id "q-110987" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}cx{e}^{y},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$\n\n- ${∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y=1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/8a94024cbce0389b1d9c60bf64a38cb7c8e8e52836b2b39e9e638f856a1c5269.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c>0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n{∬}_{{R}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}cx{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}cx{e}^{y}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}cx[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{e}^{y}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}cx[{e}^{y}]_{y=0}^{y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}cx({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}-{e}^{0})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}cx(x-1)dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(c{x}^{2}-cx)dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(c{x}^{2}-cx)dx & ={[\\frac{c{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{c{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8c}{3}-\\frac{4c}{2})-(\\frac{c}{3}-\\frac{c}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5c}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5c}{6}=1\\,⇒\\,c=\\frac{6}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-110987/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "129940fb-a409-55bc-9852-f68f4f9ffd11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-110987"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111167/selection/bc99aa5f3ee62c40cb834b274ce88683dbffd8fee8404db2b536df0189aa9cdc" :answer/id #uuid "5808f9c8-1acf-5fb2-a8aa-88a981977f72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111167/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "76aab725-61bc-5b71-a4a0-5d90f5caa286" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111167/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer/id #uuid "8318c4a5-634a-5979-804c-4ff01e5a676c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111167/selection/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde" :answer/id #uuid "91d9003e-86c2-5bfb-80eb-0bd17424d093" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111167/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f" :answer/id #uuid "a3c4a3ae-4d7f-5d2c-b91d-bfdd5c77ca88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111167/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a25ad76c-a9d6-53d3-bbfc-eacf6b7385a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-111167/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer-field/choices ["q-111167/selection/bc99aa5f3ee62c40cb834b274ce88683dbffd8fee8404db2b536df0189aa9cdc" "q-111167/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-111167/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" "q-111167/selection/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde" "q-111167/selection/0e8c61e1cbe5b6d4b3e52c0431e48b853c5faa01ca7ca0f5f9cf780292b06b1f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111167" :question/id #uuid "0ddb1c47-bdc4-5f33-8d84-507752a44afb" :question/math-academy-id "q-111167" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X+Y>1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,1]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A={X+Y>1}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/58c1beb1b13680e330260d93fdf8e60460e2bfeae4c1cbbc2fce8b261afe7ea1.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y>1) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{A}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-111167/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bcf1eb2-cf04-5dd0-bb43-682c7e9cd953"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111167"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111150/selection/f2288f9352f7ca2a51938247a89477aea196296ae7b20690ce35ebb30dfe5331" :answer/id #uuid "22fcbe0f-62c7-564c-958a-713d51b5aeac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111150/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "95a45bc7-f3a5-5017-8e6d-fde0726b3146" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111150/selection/dbc9f34791df2cfa1ba97f4fcb508d6756c3df39f1458e13c2498bf0264679fe" :answer/id #uuid "35445f75-65db-5083-899a-4a8b8c080297" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111150/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "fc45eb56-e17f-58f4-892c-3178e4e72f55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111150/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "d50e6f7c-3660-5413-8fe9-eb111f878a13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111150/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0f1d082f-9676-540b-ba2d-5f7650172353" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-111150/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-111150/selection/f2288f9352f7ca2a51938247a89477aea196296ae7b20690ce35ebb30dfe5331" "q-111150/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-111150/selection/dbc9f34791df2cfa1ba97f4fcb508d6756c3df39f1458e13c2498bf0264679fe" "q-111150/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-111150/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111150" :question/id #uuid "15866248-87b8-5440-85e9-a5b2bdb2a1b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-111150" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{xy}{4},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X<Y).$" :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,2]\\times [0,2],$ and the event $A={X<Y}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/9213a4b132f625677fcc5719e71900d037ac08088dc477f8d6a93f9ca67bc3d4.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<Y) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{xy}{4}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}\\frac{xy}{4}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}y}{8}]}_{x=0}^{x=y}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{8}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{32}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111150/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bcf1eb2-cf04-5dd0-bb43-682c7e9cd953"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111150"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111153/selection/b34544a9837d181994c7a132937df1564b327d325fab23b2c613d8bcfe8cb599" :answer/id #uuid "9b04e26a-7498-569f-ab4a-0d1d4a5a4ebf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.375" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111153/selection/43e1b12a6cc69a9cbcf7a250a6a9312a6de925ce664105c8860f9f2f5bc6be62" :answer/id #uuid "510a0901-b221-5ddd-bc99-0aaca1bb179a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.528" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111153/selection/bfb8f19753b8974e546d3a23fc7bafd18a75685d7d082be449b9e6fce6b00059" :answer/id #uuid "90f36157-0b2b-5f85-a6cd-981f05711307" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.264" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111153/selection/3278d6af787090567d72a195a3ba8dc9094d89eed1a7b027b6d298dd380fb50a" :answer/id #uuid "ea29f6d8-31d0-510e-a564-c5fe83a4a597" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.421" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111153/selection/45182a220af8f6b9897755200d5c225400cbc825a08fc1918b3dc799141b8002" :answer/id #uuid "2802c2c6-4a75-569d-901c-d452b1829484" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.132" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111153/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9ecdac5-8654-5d25-984f-915c9974dfb5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-111153/selection/bfb8f19753b8974e546d3a23fc7bafd18a75685d7d082be449b9e6fce6b00059" :answer-field/choices ["q-111153/selection/b34544a9837d181994c7a132937df1564b327d325fab23b2c613d8bcfe8cb599" "q-111153/selection/43e1b12a6cc69a9cbcf7a250a6a9312a6de925ce664105c8860f9f2f5bc6be62" "q-111153/selection/bfb8f19753b8974e546d3a23fc7bafd18a75685d7d082be449b9e6fce6b00059" "q-111153/selection/3278d6af787090567d72a195a3ba8dc9094d89eed1a7b027b6d298dd380fb50a" "q-111153/selection/45182a220af8f6b9897755200d5c225400cbc825a08fc1918b3dc799141b8002"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111153" :question/id #uuid "58a14ca3-7ee8-5b93-a4bb-5d0edad0644d" :question/math-academy-id "q-111153" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x-y},\\, & x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X+Y<1).$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,\\infty )\\times [0,\\infty ),$ and the event $A={X+Y<1}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/df0bf32b4785a9f43946bd3b08f1b255549485f2275c74607fb5285e2b1baa3c.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y<1) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-y}{e}^{-x-y}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-y}{e}^{-x-y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[-{e}^{-x-y}]_{x=0}^{x=1-y}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{-y}-{e}^{-1})\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[-{e}^{-y}-{e}^{-1}y]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1}-{e}^{-1}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{e-2}{e} \\\\  & ≈0.264.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111153/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bcf1eb2-cf04-5dd0-bb43-682c7e9cd953"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111153"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111163/selection/9700accffa78065d8053126335d2ac4e2336d0d88c76df9e6a237030f752585a" :answer/id #uuid "71e3af58-e13f-548e-98d9-16143300261b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111163/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" :answer/id #uuid "9aee4e20-a13b-59fe-a62b-1da5e771baca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111163/selection/aec3de9a3ef8747c1a1f08fed4b987384e92acb8f2ff9b5e9f83b6456734e6aa" :answer/id #uuid "f19b1722-22f8-57cf-b8e0-9ecc213abb90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{27}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111163/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "37609cdf-d9fe-5671-9c36-cb27c3a2123b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111163/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "ca4ee91d-9521-50b4-b2ce-fa65fa7a62e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111163/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed563015-d856-5448-bfc8-c5bb1d5eedc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-111163/selection/9700accffa78065d8053126335d2ac4e2336d0d88c76df9e6a237030f752585a" :answer-field/choices ["q-111163/selection/9700accffa78065d8053126335d2ac4e2336d0d88c76df9e6a237030f752585a" "q-111163/selection/9c6bfb4db8d042ca3b93589c844ac1c789909e0099f428d8083546a00b4d8cf7" "q-111163/selection/aec3de9a3ef8747c1a1f08fed4b987384e92acb8f2ff9b5e9f83b6456734e6aa" "q-111163/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-111163/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111163" :question/id #uuid "9d00d275-db06-5f3f-ae74-29e8404f94a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-111163" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{(1+x+y)^{3}},\\, & 0\\le y\\le x, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X+Y<2).$" :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D={0\\le y\\le x},$ and the event $A={X+Y<2}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/f7a0f0fb9d20a4b88d0aa4c395e2adb1d62195601ce756f57a48becc6ab38681.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X+Y<2) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}\\frac{4}{(1+x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}\\frac{4}{(1+x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[-\\frac{2}{(1+x+y)^{2}}]}_{x=y}^{x=2-y}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{2}{(1+2y)^{2}}-\\frac{2}{9})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{1+2y}-\\frac{2y}{9}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{2}{9}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-111163/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bcf1eb2-cf04-5dd0-bb43-682c7e9cd953"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111163"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-111168/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "1ac374d1-a06d-5413-8c63-093fd7926fbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111168/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "884b235e-bd56-54fe-a8c8-92aae9b99a4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111168/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "1ee1b383-54ed-5337-b40b-e20fbe70c185" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111168/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "125d44d8-164e-5a44-b2ee-1023420682da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111168/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "dd8174b2-2ab8-5de1-b2db-831966c2c823" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-111168/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "649f2cd5-cd81-5072-b669-229c939ef6c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-111168/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-111168/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-111168/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-111168/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-111168/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-111168/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-111168" :question/id #uuid "efd49b5c-a9f8-5477-b8d0-3a01e093397c" :question/math-academy-id "q-111168" :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(X>1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,2]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A={X>1}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/26cbd44827c3a5a3fde5d61b631ce4f214bcf9a36ce6bf76129b1fe9f9478eff.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{A}\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-111168/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2bcf1eb2-cf04-5dd0-bb43-682c7e9cd953"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-111168"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9207"] :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/a1b3940558e5a6d90d2911c18571eb91d63a4baa63bbe467fb8359c6fa5f44ea.png)\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y) \\geq 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint_{\\mathbb R^2} f(x,y) \\;\\textrm{d}x\\textrm{d}y= 1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D = \\left\\{(x,y) \\::\\:  0\\lt x\\lt \\dfrac{\\pi}{2},0\\lt y \\lt \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} \\right\\}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/ccb7cc52f8404dcca5d555d4fd81e6ae03e9689ccdd7c462fccbc2dc611db235.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c > 0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y) \\geq 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2}\\int_{0}^{\\pi/2}c\\sin (x+y) \\;\\textrm{d}y\\,\\textrm{d}x= 1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}c\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & =c{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =c{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)]_{y=0}^{y=\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =c{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =c{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =c{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =c[(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}))] \\\\  & =c[(1-0)-(0-1)] \\\\  & =c[1-(-1)] \\\\  & =2c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n2c=1 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad c=\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9183"] :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/bba3d767c1001256f5bd4bd9bbf38059054dee21ff51714f1d3ed463f431a6c3.png)\nwhere $c$ is a positive real number. Find the value of $c.$" :question/worked-solution "To verify that $f(x,y)$ is a valid joint probability density function, we must check the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x,y) \\geq 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint_{\\mathbb R^2} f(x,y) \\;\\textrm{d}x\\,\\textrm{d}y= 1$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region $D = \\{(x,y) \\::\\: 0 \\leq x \\lt y \\}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/9c823d67872095514c6392038ff43497512de656e28b26160465760df0faa4ea.png)\n\nNow, let's check our conditions:\n\n- Since $c > 0,$ we clearly have $f(x,y) \\geq 0$ for all $(x,y)\\in \\mathbb R^2.$ So the first condition is satisfied.\n\n- For the second condition to be satisfied, we must have \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iint_{\\mathbb R^2} f(x,y) \\;\\textrm{d}x\\textrm{d}y = \\iint_{D} f(x,y) \\;\\textrm{d}x\\textrm{d}y = \\int_{0}^{\\infty}\\int_{x}^{\\infty} \\dfrac{c}{(1+x+y)^3} \\;\\textrm{d}y\\,\\textrm{d}x= 1.\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating  $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }[{\\int }_{x}^{\\infty }\\frac{c}{(1+x+y)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & =c{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }[{\\int }_{x}^{\\infty }(1+x+y)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =c{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{[-\\frac{1}{2}(1+x+y)^{-2}]}_{y=x}^{y=\\infty }\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{c}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{[(1+x+y)^{-2}]}_{y=x}^{y=\\infty }\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{c}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }0-(1+2x)^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{c}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }-(1+2x)^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(1+2x)^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{c}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(1+2x)^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{c}{2}{[-\\frac{1}{2}(1+2x)^{-1}]}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-\\frac{c}{4}{[\\frac{1}{1+2x}]}_{0}^{\\infty } \\\\  & =-\\frac{c}{4}[0-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{c}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{c}{4}=1 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad c=4.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9184"] :question/problem "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/f7aed2445b7b518afecd13a5979a873b8bfc17e8eb1ff8d41f4a0d9c912deaf4.png)\n\nFind $P(X > 1, Y < 1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A\\subset \\mathbb R^2,$ then\n\n$$\nP\\left((X,Y)\\in A\\right) = \\iint_A f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d x\\textrm d y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D = [0,3]\\times [0,2],$ and the event $A = \\left\\{ X > 1, Y < 1\\right\\}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14062830/assets/b1fc6548c909b9887c708c4c5dcce5b715d112defc7ce1fc639784bbaf55e111.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1,Y<1) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{∬}_{A}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot (3-1)\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
